    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nWhen using mini.ai with an XML file that has nested tags with the same name, the text objects don't respect their scope.\r\nFor example:\r\n<group>\r\n    <group>\r\n    </group>\r\n</group\r\nif the command \"vit\" is used on the outermost tag, only the word <group>(on line 2) will be selected.\r\nIt would be better, in my opinion, if mini.ai selected both middle lines instead.\r\n",
